      "invalidCitations": 0,
      "ttftMs": 48570.677995000005,
      "endToEndMs": 49567,
      "finishReason": "stop",
      "modelText": "Hi,\n\nYou do not have to keep every Nimbus file on your computer, as two features help you save disk space [3].\n\nWith online-only files, every file and folder appears on your computer, but only takes up space when you open it [1]. You can right-click a file and choose Make online-only to free up its space [1]. These files require an internet connection to open, and the feature is available on Windows 10 and later and macOS 12.3 and later [1].\n\nAlternatively, selective sync lets you choose which folders appear on your computer at all [2]. You can go to Preferences > Sync > Choose folders and untick folders you do not need, which removes them from your computer while keeping them safe in your account [2]. On Linux, you should use selective sync [1].",
      "calls": 1,
      "latencyMs": 49535.83009,
      "inputTokens": 912,
      "outputTokens": 477,
      "estCostMicros": 2473,
      "providerErrors": []
